\ A runtime definition shadowing a dictionary native. The collision sits inside a word body called
\ from top level, so it fires while the file runs rather than at parse time, and an AOT build of
\ this file reaches it at binary runtime instead of during the freeze.
\
\ The `use` gives the entry file an import. The bare call is the file's last statement, so the
\ raise stays in tail position on every tier. No caller frame row forks the rendering. A
\ configuration that accepts the shadow in silence shows as exit 0 with an empty stderr.

use { taken: } "def_over_import_mod.1z" ;

taken .

shadow-native: ( -- ) [ dup: ( -- x ) [ 0 ] ; ] ;

shadow-native
